       Details of the signal handling are obscure and differ between  systems.
       The  BSD  man  page  states:  "To  avoid a possible deadlock situation,
       processes that are children in the middle of a vvffoorrkk() are  never  sent
       SSIIGGTTTTOOUU  or  SSIIGGTTTTIINN  signals; rather, output or _i_o_c_t_ls are allowed and
       input attempts result in an end‐of‐file indication."

